17
00:01:23,336 --> 00:01:24,936
Order flow continuation setups.

18
00:01:25,036 --> 00:01:26,136
This is lesson 17.

19
00:01:26,236 --> 00:01:29,936
The market spends a majority of the time trending from one price extreme to another.

20
00:01:30,636 --> 00:01:32,336
The big money is made in trends.

21
00:01:32,436 --> 00:01:35,936
You always hear about the trend followers, the turtle, trend system.

22
00:01:36,936 --> 00:01:38,936
You know, that's great.

23
00:01:40,036 --> 00:01:44,236
If you're a long-term trader, but most people are shorter-term traders.

24
00:01:44,536 --> 00:01:50,336
They don't have the big capital behind them that the big funds have that they can sit on a trend for six months.

25
00:01:50,336 --> 00:01:53,836
However, the good news is that trends appear intraday as well.

26
00:01:55,136 --> 00:01:59,236
When the market is in the middle of a big move, no one can tell you how long or how far it will go.

27
00:01:59,636 --> 00:02:02,236
What you want to know is whether it's going to continue or not.

28
00:02:02,436 --> 00:02:09,436
So whether it's a trend on a one-minute chart or a trend on a daily chart or a monthly chart,

29
00:02:11,876 --> 00:02:14,276
You don't know when it's going to end, how far it's going to go.

30
00:02:14,776 --> 00:02:27,976
What you want to do is you want to identify that there is a trend and jump on board and try and catch your berries, catch your grapes, pick your low-hanging fruit

31
00:02:29,176 --> 00:02:29,976
when it's happening.

32
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:36,776
So in order flow, I have four continuation steps.

33
00:02:36,776 --> 00:02:40,176
It's really three, but one's worded as two.

34
00:02:40,576 --> 00:02:48,476
Basically, it's big fat market imbalance, stacked buying imbalance, or stacked selling imbalance, or what I like to call the three in a row.

35
00:02:49,076 --> 00:02:50,876
And I'll show you.

36
00:02:51,076 --> 00:02:55,476
It's easier to see it, I think, with photos. But quickly, I'll just explain it.

37
00:02:55,476 --> 00:02:59,076
A big fat market imbalance occurs when there is an oversized market imbalance.

38
00:02:59,976 --> 00:03:06,776
High volume levels are common at the beginning of moves and in the middle of moves, and bigger, well-funded institutional traders start to come into the market.

39
00:03:07,176 --> 00:03:09,176
So what that means is...

40
00:03:09,776 --> 00:03:11,376
You know, a market has turned, okay?

41
00:03:11,676 --> 00:03:17,176
It's reached its low or reached its high, and it's starting to move in the opposite direction.

42
00:03:17,276 --> 00:03:18,276
A reversal has started.

43
00:03:18,976 --> 00:03:22,776
And, you know, the reversal is going to be the beginning of the trend.

44
00:03:23,076 --> 00:03:25,476
Well, how do you know the trend is starting to pick up steam?

45
00:03:25,976 --> 00:03:35,376
Is when you see, you know, the big players come in and, you know, build their position up, whether it's, you know, they're building their position up on the long side or the short side.

46
00:03:35,776 --> 00:03:36,976
Sometimes they...

47
00:03:39,776 --> 00:03:42,276
and you can see it really clearly in the order flow.

48
00:03:42,776 --> 00:03:44,776
Is it in a normal bar chart? You wouldn't see it.

49
00:03:45,276 --> 00:03:53,676
But, you know, for example, okay, so I like to think it's easier to explain things when you have a picture of a chart in front of you.

50
00:03:53,676 --> 00:03:56,076
So I'll talk about the big fat market imbalance.

51
00:03:56,576 --> 00:03:59,976
Now, when you're trading a market, you should know what's considered...

52
00:04:00,276 --> 00:04:10,276
Big volume when it goes through, so you can determine if there's institutional participation or not.

53
00:04:10,676 --> 00:04:18,976
So for E-mini S&Ps, I tend to look at volume between 50 and

54
00:04:20,276 --> 00:04:21,676
2,000 is kind of normal.

55
00:04:21,876 --> 00:04:30,376
Once you start getting above 2,500, to me that's really big size going through, at least the beginning of big size.

56
00:04:31,476 --> 00:04:34,376
And especially on a five range chart, that moves very fast.

57
00:04:34,676 --> 00:04:38,376
If I'm seeing imbalances, if I'm seeing bars with volume over

58
00:04:39,576 --> 00:04:50,376
you know, two and a half thousand, you know, I'm starting to pay attention because, you know, someone has got size, they're moving on both sides, you know, to

59
00:04:51,276 --> 00:05:00,576
see a price level where you got, you know, over two thousand, two and a half thousand, it's saying that, you know, even though there's an active buyer, there's still an active seller.

60
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:07,676
Now when I see an imbalance above 2,500, then I really stand and pay attention and I usually take a trade.

61
00:05:07,976 --> 00:05:13,676
So here you see... A big imbalance, 2,800, you know, as the market's going up.

62
00:05:14,476 --> 00:05:17,376
You know, you're not going to necessarily see that on a low of a move.

63
00:05:17,376 --> 00:05:22,576
You tend to find, you know, the imbalances going in your direction of the trend.

64
00:05:23,276 --> 00:05:26,876
You know, not necessarily, you know, when you're going up.

65
00:05:27,376 --> 00:05:39,676
When you want to see aggressive buying, you're not going to all of a sudden start to go up, up, up, up, up, and on your move up, have aggressive selling, because there's going to be people bidding the market, there's going to be people buying the offer.

66
00:05:40,276 --> 00:05:46,676
Generally, on a move up, You're going to have people buying the offer being aggressive. That's why you should see buying imbalances.

67
00:05:47,176 --> 00:05:49,776
On a move down, you should be seeing selling imbalances.

68
00:05:50,176 --> 00:05:57,476
But when you see a number that really stands out here, 2,800, you know, it's blue. It's a buying imbalance. You know, it's against 480.

69
00:05:57,576 --> 00:06:02,976
It's telling me, you know, There was some size there, but people were extremely aggressive and lifted the offer.

70
00:06:03,376 --> 00:06:05,776
It could have been one person. It could have been a couple people. Who knows?

71
00:06:06,176 --> 00:06:13,176
But the fact is, it didn't spend much time at these levels. It traded here. It went bid here and traded higher.

72
00:06:14,776 --> 00:06:17,376
You get a selling imbalance up here of 2,000.

73
00:06:17,776 --> 00:06:25,276
Okay, it's big, but it's just sort of on the borderline of average to big.

74
00:06:26,176 --> 00:06:29,776
And it's not uncommon to get a selling imbalance just off of a high.

75
00:06:30,376 --> 00:06:34,576
Especially in a red bar because the market is going to go bid and it's going to trade back and forth.

76
00:06:34,676 --> 00:06:39,776
Lots of times you're going to get smaller volume traded right up on the high of a red bar, just as, you know,

77
00:06:39,876 --> 00:06:46,976
In a green candle, it's very common to get a buying imbalance on the second slot just off the low.

78
00:06:48,076 --> 00:06:50,676
These are normal occurrences.

79
00:06:50,776 --> 00:06:57,976
Just like you have this buying imbalance here, you have this selling imbalance here, here you have this selling imbalance. It's just sort of how the market trades.

80
00:06:58,276 --> 00:07:02,776
Oftentimes, as I said, at the bottom of a green candle, you tend to get smaller volume.

81
00:07:04,076 --> 00:07:06,676
So it's not uncommon to get the imbalance.

82
00:07:06,876 --> 00:07:14,076
Here you have the imbalance again. So I'm not too concerned with it, you know, as opposed to when I see a big number sticking out in the middle.

83
00:07:18,744 --> 00:07:25,044
Okay, a stacked buying imbalance occurs when there's three or more buying imbalances in the bar stacked on top of each other.

84
00:07:25,144 --> 00:07:30,344
Stacked selling imbalance occurs when there are three or more selling imbalances in a bar stacked on top of each other.

85
00:07:31,444 --> 00:07:34,144
And, you know, again, it's...

86
00:07:34,844 --> 00:07:46,444
Due to the importance is it's due to above average volume aggressive traders coming into the market to move it the majority of the time is one trader but it can be several traders at the same time coming into the market to move it

87
00:07:47,644 --> 00:07:55,144
you know oftentimes you're what you're seeing is the result of a big order coming into the market that has to be executed as the market's moving

88
00:07:56,344 --> 00:08:08,344
So what you have here, this is in the E-minis, this is at 720 in the morning, and you see in the stacked buying imbalance, you have three in a row right here, they're all stacked on top of each other.

89
00:08:08,644 --> 00:08:14,244
Here you have four in a row, and you're looking for the market to continue in that trend.

90
00:08:14,644 --> 00:08:19,444
What you're seeing is, in this case, in times when there's...

91
00:08:20,244 --> 00:08:32,044
I'll say it's an illiquid time, but 7.20 in the morning tends to be lesser volume than after 8.30 once the cash opens.

92
00:08:32,144 --> 00:08:33,644
But it's still important nevertheless.

93
00:08:33,644 --> 00:08:37,244
What you're seeing here is someone's got a big order they're trying to execute.

94
00:08:37,644 --> 00:08:38,944
They start buying some here.

95
00:08:38,944 --> 00:08:39,944
They're a little bit aggressive.

96
00:08:39,944 --> 00:08:41,144
You see the buying and balances.

97
00:08:41,144 --> 00:08:42,144
The market never comes back.

98
00:08:42,544 --> 00:08:44,044
Then we start trading a little bit higher.

99
00:08:44,144 --> 00:08:45,044
Now they're getting a little bit higher.

100
00:08:44,644 --> 00:08:45,444
more aggressive.

101
00:08:46,144 --> 00:08:48,444
Why is a buy-in, stack buy-in and balance important?

102
00:08:48,544 --> 00:08:51,544
Well, the market's trading here at $18.89.

103
00:08:52,044 --> 00:08:55,544
Someone's got probably $1,000, $1,005 to buy.

104
00:08:56,744 --> 00:09:01,944
They just go in. They know they're going to move the market a bit, but they want to get it done pretty quick.

105
00:09:02,844 --> 00:09:07,844
S&Ps is one of those markets where you can move. You know, a thousand and maybe move at a point.

106
00:09:08,844 --> 00:09:11,644
So, you know, they're going to be aggressive and just go in and get it done.

107
00:09:12,144 --> 00:09:20,544
Now, you know, the market will oftentimes squirt up a little bit, you know, as other buyers come into the market and say, hey, we just rallied a point and I want to start buying.

108
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:25,444
When the market retraces back into that zone of the buying imbalance,

109
00:09:26,244 --> 00:09:30,444
You're looking to see if there's going to be additional buyers in this area.

110
00:09:30,644 --> 00:09:32,944
That's when you're going to see a continuation of the move.

111
00:09:33,344 --> 00:09:43,144
If it's just a one-time order where someone was working against a basket of stocks or something and they just had to get it done and got it done, yeah, the market may trade sideways and then come off.

112
00:09:43,444 --> 00:09:46,544
But if it's a legitimate...

113
00:09:46,744 --> 00:10:00,344
Trend and the imbalance is legitimate where it's just somebody you know they want to build their position oftentimes when you pull into the imbalance it will trade around there and then continue on in its trend like you see here

114
00:10:03,616 --> 00:10:07,616
Often times it takes a lot to get a market to move outside of a trading range and start a trend.

115
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:15,616
Once the market starts a trend, the forces behind the move often appear in the order flow to confirm the move. Then you know that move will continue.

116
00:10:16,916 --> 00:10:29,416
So like I said, it's one of those things I hate to call a self-fulfilling prophecy, but when traders think the market's going to move, they're always talking to other people and trying to talk up their position.

117
00:10:30,916 --> 00:10:32,816
In hopes to get the market to continue.

118
00:10:33,116 --> 00:10:38,616
I mean, it doesn't always work that way, but there's obviously big supply and demand factors in there.

119
00:10:39,116 --> 00:10:40,416
But once a trend starts,

120
00:10:42,316 --> 00:10:48,216
Look for the order flow to confirm that the move has happened and get in and take advantage of that move.

121
00:10:52,460 --> 00:10:57,660
Okay, the next continuation setup is what I call the three in a row.

122
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:02,860
The three in a row occurs when you have three ratios in a row in the same direction.

123
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:10,660
Basically, you want to look to get in after the third bar that you see the ratio. Your entry could be anywhere between the point of control and the second and third bars.

124
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:14,960
What it looks like is this. You have ratio, ratio, ratio.

125
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:18,060
I'm not necessarily concerned about this buying imbalance.

126
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:23,960
It's nice to see, but normally you don't get also a buying imbalance or a selling imbalance in your three in a row.

127
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:32,060
What you're really concerned with is the ratios. And it doesn't have to be a ratio balance low, small print, small print or anything like that.

128
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:39,360
As long as there's three blue numbers, it could be single print, single print, single print. It could be... Large print, single print, small print.

129
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,460
It doesn't really matter.

130
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:45,060
What I'm really concerned about is having three ratios in a row.

131
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:48,660
And, you know, like this, I could just sort of walk you through it real quick.

132
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:54,060
You have a ratio balance low, so it's heavy volume down here. And the market starts rallying.

133
00:11:54,060 --> 00:12:01,560
You get a single print. You know, it's... The sellers in this bar are rejecting the lower prices. That's why you have the single print.

134
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:02,760
The market goes higher.

135
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:07,760
This one is technically a ratio balance low, but it's close to a single print.

136
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:14,360
But again, the sellers are rejecting the lower prices down here, and the market continues on higher.

137
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,560
Really what's important is you have one, two, three.

138
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:32,960
blue numbers in a row or you know on a down moving market if they're up above the red bars where your point of entry is it's somewhere you know between these two points of controls between the third bar and the second bar

139
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:37,460
You want to get a little bit of a pullback for a better entry.

140
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:48,660
There's going to be times where it just continues on and you miss your entry, but I prefer to have a little bit of wiggle room by getting a better entry rather than just paying the market.

141
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:53,660
So a continuation pattern allows you to find an entry point in an existing trend.

142
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:58,060
Trends aren't where the big money is made in trading, so it's to your benefit to jump in on the trend.

143
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:03,360
Some traders base their entire trading program on just jumping along for the ride.

144
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:06,760
So it'll benefit you to have a few continuation pattern setups to look for.

145
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:15,760
Like I said, some of these hedge funds and CTAs that have been around for 20, 30 years are trend followers.

146
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:20,160
They're not trying to pick tops and bottoms.

147
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:25,660
They just want to identify when a trend is occurring and ride it for as long as they can.

148
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:32,260
These guys, that's why they trade 50, 60 different markets around the world.

149
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:33,660
They're looking for the...

150
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:39,160
Six or seven or eight markets a year that have the monster trends where they're going to make up all their money.

151
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:45,760
That's why they're willing to take a bunch of small losses, but their winner is going to be quite big.

152
00:13:49,092 --> 00:13:53,192
So when a trend is underway and there's a pattern telling you to buy, you buy.

153
00:13:53,292 --> 00:13:59,092
Just as if the market is telling you to sell, you sell, especially in a trend.

154
00:13:59,192 --> 00:14:07,092
You want to ride the trend because when the market moves from a low to a high and you're not in on it, you feel like an idiot.

155
00:14:07,692 --> 00:14:11,692
But you still need a reason to get into the trade.

156
00:14:12,292 --> 00:14:15,492
All right, so... Let's take a look at a chart.

157
00:14:15,792 --> 00:14:17,092
Here you have a bond chart.

158
00:14:17,192 --> 00:14:19,292
We came into the low at 11.45.

159
00:14:19,292 --> 00:14:24,592
You have the single print. Then, you know, 30 minutes later you have another single print.

160
00:14:24,792 --> 00:14:29,792
So now you're sort of convinced yourself that the trend is up, that we're starting to move away.

161
00:14:30,392 --> 00:14:31,892
Where's your continuation pattern?

162
00:14:31,992 --> 00:14:34,592
You come back down to the same level, it holds.

163
00:14:34,692 --> 00:14:42,692
Then you're starting to see, you know, as you're moving up, you're starting to see confirmation with single print, single print, and the market moves higher.

164
00:14:46,852 --> 00:14:50,452
This one's a little bit more messy, but nevertheless, I'll talk about it.

165
00:14:50,952 --> 00:14:56,352
We sort of peaked up here at 1018 in the bonds and start coming down.

166
00:14:56,852 --> 00:15:03,252
You have a ratio here of 0.53, and the market proceeds to go sideways.

167
00:15:06,552 --> 00:15:12,252
I know the high is here, and what's happening is you're starting to get a couple ratios here, a couple ratios here.

168
00:15:12,752 --> 00:15:17,952
It's kind of hard to really get a good gauge on which way the market's going to go.

169
00:15:18,152 --> 00:15:21,052
So what I'm looking at is where the points of controls are.

170
00:15:21,652 --> 00:15:24,652
Now, I know points of control here, here, here.

171
00:15:24,952 --> 00:15:29,552
I had talked about earlier using point of controls as support or resistance.

172
00:15:30,052 --> 00:15:37,552
So in this case, I'm using, I think the market is in a downtrend because I know we have a high here and I see this ratio bounce low.

173
00:15:38,952 --> 00:15:46,652
Even though you have a single print here, a large print here, but you have opposing single prints just on the other side of these two.

174
00:15:46,952 --> 00:15:51,652
But what's interesting is you have the points of controls all lining up right here.

175
00:15:51,952 --> 00:15:58,152
You know, so now... I'm not too concerned about these because this one still has a negative delta.

176
00:15:58,152 --> 00:15:59,952
This one has a small positive delta.

177
00:16:00,552 --> 00:16:05,152
If I'm expecting the market to really move higher, I want to see a strong positive delta.

178
00:16:05,752 --> 00:16:10,952
So, you know, I'm able to take this ratio, this ratio, this ratio more seriously than these two.

179
00:16:11,252 --> 00:16:13,052
In fact, I got the points of controls here.

180
00:16:13,652 --> 00:16:17,152
I'm still looking for a downtrend. I'm still looking for the market to move lower.

181
00:16:17,652 --> 00:16:23,552
Then I'm seeing a few more confirmation ratios here, ratio bounce low and single print.

182
00:16:23,852 --> 00:16:26,352
So it's telling me the move should be lower.

183
00:16:30,252 --> 00:16:35,552
Again, this is the bond, and you hit the high, and we start working our way down.

184
00:16:35,552 --> 00:16:40,052
You're seeing the single prints here with nice ratio, 77, 82.

185
00:16:41,552 --> 00:16:46,552
And you're thinking already the trend is lower.

186
00:16:47,152 --> 00:16:49,952
You know, maybe you're not convinced yet. You want a little bit extra.

187
00:16:50,252 --> 00:16:54,852
But, you know, you're seeing the selling imbalances, selling imbalance, selling imbalance, selling imbalance, selling imbalance.

188
00:16:55,352 --> 00:17:02,452
You know, if you're still not convinced, this bar here has got a very strong negative delta. And then immediately it's followed by a bar with a single print.

189
00:17:02,852 --> 00:17:07,252
So it's telling you, you know, you should have been alert way up here.

190
00:17:07,452 --> 00:17:11,652
But, you know, we're in the trend already. So you're looking for a sign of continuation.

191
00:17:12,052 --> 00:17:14,452
You're seeing a delta very strong.

192
00:17:14,552 --> 00:17:16,152
You're seeing a lot of selling imbalances.

193
00:17:16,652 --> 00:17:21,852
You're seeing the single print to help confirm the move lower.

194
00:17:25,988 --> 00:17:30,288
Okay, now this is an E-mini chart. Now, we've come down into our low here.

195
00:17:30,488 --> 00:17:32,088
We've got a buying imbalance right on the low.

196
00:17:32,388 --> 00:17:37,088
Okay, maybe you're not yet convinced that this is the low. You want to see the trend start to happen before getting in.

197
00:17:37,488 --> 00:17:42,688
And boom, you get this other ratio bounce low here indicating some stopping volume.

198
00:17:43,088 --> 00:17:47,488
And you get another buying imbalance, you know, and the market worked its way back up.

199
00:17:51,588 --> 00:17:55,288
Okay, S&Ps again. We're working our way lower.

200
00:17:57,396 --> 00:18:00,996
You know, we got a ratio balance low, some heavy volume here. We got a single print.

201
00:18:02,496 --> 00:18:04,796
You get a pullback up to the single print, okay.

202
00:18:05,396 --> 00:18:07,496
You know you're working your way lower. You get a pullback.

203
00:18:08,596 --> 00:18:13,196
You know, well, you know, I'm not sure if this is a pullback or we're just going to go higher.

204
00:18:13,496 --> 00:18:15,196
So you want to have some extra confirmation.

205
00:18:15,296 --> 00:18:15,796
Now you have it.

206
00:18:15,896 --> 00:18:18,196
You have the selling imbalance and the market sells off.

207
00:18:20,096 --> 00:18:26,296
This by itself, where we trace back up to the single print for me, is normally a good trade.

208
00:18:26,596 --> 00:18:28,996
I like it when the market circles back up to a single print.

209
00:18:30,296 --> 00:18:36,896
If you get short, then when I see a sell and a balance, it tells me to hold on to the trade a bit longer.

210
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:44,160
Okay, so, you know, we're working our way up.

211
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:49,560
Nice ratios here, blueprints. It's telling you we're in a trend already.

212
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,860
You really should have been looking to get long in here.

213
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:57,460
Say you missed it. You're looking for another reason to get long that the trend is going to keep continuing.

214
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:00,460
And what do you have? You've got buying imbalance here.

215
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:04,660
I'm usually not a big... Person to get long in a buying imbalance.

216
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:10,460
But you know what? This is one of those cases where if you have a tight stop, you know, I usually like to get long in a buying imbalance.

217
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,860
I'd prefer to get a little bit lower though.

218
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:21,260
You know, but if you have a tight stop, you can manage it and, you know, it's going to give you a chance to get back in on the move back up.

219
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:25,060
Like I said, you have this high here with the ratio of single print.

220
00:19:27,524 --> 00:19:36,924
sort of standing in your way, but you know what, if you're able to get in somewhere down here, you know, your risk is relatively low, because usually I like to see a pull back up to this level.

221
00:19:37,324 --> 00:19:42,324
So, you know, if you're going to get a pull back up to that level, you could have a chance to get past it, you know.

222
00:19:43,524 --> 00:19:50,224
Sometimes it's hard to sell a high, just off of a single print and a ratio and negative delta, but...

223
00:19:50,924 --> 00:19:52,824
You know, there are times when it doesn't work.

224
00:19:53,024 --> 00:19:55,424
And, you know, if you're looking for a continuation of a trend,

225
00:19:58,588 --> 00:20:00,088
then it's going to happen.

226
00:20:02,988 --> 00:20:04,188
That one made no sense.

227
00:20:05,688 --> 00:20:07,788
Okay, now what do you have here? You got an E-mini chart.

228
00:20:07,788 --> 00:20:09,088
Markets coming down, down, down.

229
00:20:09,088 --> 00:20:11,088
You got a couple selling imbalances right in a row.

230
00:20:11,688 --> 00:20:15,488
Now this is, I like this, where you get two selling imbalances split over two bars.

231
00:20:17,588 --> 00:20:20,688
You get the pullback up here in a single print, and then the market sells off.

232
00:20:20,788 --> 00:20:22,988
You know, when you're seeing selling imbalances,

233
00:20:24,988 --> 00:20:32,788
going into a low, you might want to be careful, but if you get a pullback in there, it's telling you that these most likely are going to hold and the market's going to continue lower.

234
00:20:35,632 --> 00:20:37,532
Again, we had sort of coming off our high up here.

235
00:20:37,632 --> 00:20:43,932
We got a selling imbalance. Then you're seeing the confirmation with the ratios, the blue numbers, as the market's moving lower.

236
00:20:47,032 --> 00:20:50,432
So this is the end of lesson 17, continuation setups.

237
00:20:51,332 --> 00:20:57,732
In the next lesson, I'll explain how to integrate order flow with your traditional technical analysis to enhance your current ways of trading.

238
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:02,432
I didn't spend much time under continuation setups because...

239
00:21:04,632 --> 00:21:07,232
It should be pretty easy, I think, for you to spot.

240
00:21:07,632 --> 00:21:09,632
I gave you a few setups that I like to look for.

241
00:21:10,032 --> 00:21:15,732
But in general, you're still looking for the same things that you're looking for around reversals.

242
00:21:16,532 --> 00:21:24,232
With continuations, it's generally because you missed the reversal sign and you're getting in just a little bit late on the continuation.

243
00:21:24,732 --> 00:21:27,732
But you should always be looking for...

244
00:21:28,532 --> 00:21:33,132
Any setups where they're occurring, just take them into context with where the market is.

245
00:21:33,532 --> 00:21:37,832
Um, If the market is trending, it's okay to take the setups.

246
00:21:38,532 --> 00:21:42,232
If the market is going sideways, I'm a bit hesitant to take setups.

247
00:21:43,632 --> 00:21:48,732
I said I want a market to be moving, not... Basically spinning its wheels.

248
00:21:49,632 --> 00:21:53,132
You know, when a market's moving is when you're going to have the opportunity to make money.

249
00:21:53,632 --> 00:21:58,932
So the important thing is, you know, just be able to determine when the market is moving, and if you're seeing a setup, take it.

250
00:21:59,032 --> 00:22:02,832
If the market is not moving and you see a setup, be hesitant.

251
00:22:04,532 --> 00:22:07,032
So thank you. That's the end of lesson 17.

